        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "HSK 4: speak",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Explain a social choice with a reason and a relevant contrast. State whose intention is known, and avoid replacing the participants’ statements with a guess.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "故意",
                "pinyin": "gùyì",
                "meaning": "deliberately; on purpose",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "4c1a6a59a329f8cf574ae545fba0aedc3cd1ee642f78d41b47eda6a777df8ef5"
              },
              {
                "text": "互相",
                "pinyin": "hùxiāng",
                "meaning": "each other; mutually",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "1d47e6e8dc0f9eb26dde5ba68e1e8e8591f68e7acdd02ea895e1e99ba7b0bc25"
              },
              {
                "text": "因为",
                "pinyin": "yīnwèi",
                "meaning": "because; owing to",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "9f45c18a9e0e1057de861448bc1f80a947cfae6803d918333f62b3c109d066ba"
              },
              {
                "text": "但是",
                "pinyin": "dànshì",
                "meaning": "but; however",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "1fac104a345a55d1bf1705e3cb2765411e111844ef0ed8389208c90fc1d31949"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Two students chose to help one another because one did not understand the lesson. Both said they wanted to help. After their attempt, that student still did not understand. Explain the reason for the choice and the contrasting result without turning failure into deliberate harm.\nFamiliar meanings available: deliberately; on purpose; each other; mutually; because; owing to; but; however."
          }
        ]
      },
