            "promptLanguage": "en",
            "context": "Two students chose to help one another because one did not understand the lesson. Both said they wanted to help. After their attempt, that student still did not understand. Explain the reason for the choice and the contrasting result without turning failure into deliberate harm.\nFamiliar meanings available: deliberately; on purpose; each other; mutually; because; owing to; but; however.",
